\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 The nine masses that weve managed to measure for the fermion particles look ratther random, as some multiverse models predict, suggesting that we\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92ll never manage to calculate them from first principles. }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Guth - when we discover an object in nature, the scientific thing to do is look for a mechanism that created it. Cars are created by car factoreies, rabbits and solar systems are created from gravitational collapse in ginat molecular clouds. So its reasonable to assume that our universe was created by some sort of universe creation mechanism. All other mechanisms naturally produce *many* copies of whatever they create; a cosmos containing only one car, one rabbit, one solar system would seem quite contrived. In the same vein, its arguably more antural for the correct universe-creation mechansim to create many universes rather than just one.}
